  "summary": "Gov. Gavin Newsom announced that the California Highway Patrol has entered an agreement with Flock Safety to install 480 ALPR cameras in Oakland and along East Bay freeways, with CHP operating them and sharing access with OPD and allied agencies. The article notes prior Oakland-Flock plans, Flock's Bay Area expansion, and civil-liberties critiques.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "CHP has entered into an agreement with the surveillance company Flock Safety to install 290 cameras around surface streets in Oakland and another 190 along state highways throughout the East Bay.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "California law makes it illegal for public agencies to share data with out-of-state police and other agencies, but the ACLU and Electronic Frontier Foundation have discovered that this is being done by some law enforcement departments.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    }
  ],
